---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import ArticleSchema from '../../components/ArticleSchema.astro';
import FaqSection from '../../components/FaqSection.astro';
import { site, pageTitle } from '../../content';
const path = '/use-cases/black-friday';
const title = pageTitle(site, 'use-cases/black-friday');
const desc = "Plan one coordinated sale across campaigns and automations, with enforceable access terms, current purchaser suppression and a named pause owner.";
const faqs = [
  {
    "question": "How many Black Friday emails should I send?",
    "answer": "Choose an audience-specific contact budget across campaigns and automations. Each message needs a purpose, and the budget should respond to current delivery and customer feedback."
  },
  {
    "question": "Should I stop all lifecycle automations?",
    "answer": "Review each one for offer and audience collisions. Adapt or pause conflicting promotions while retaining necessary order and service communication."
  },
  {
    "question": "Does high sale revenue prove the program worked?",
    "answer": "No. Review contribution, returns, delivery health and comparable repeat-purchase cohorts. Attribution alone does not measure incremental impact."
  }
];
---

<BaseLayout title={title} description={desc} site={site} path={path}>
  <ArticleSchema title={title} description={desc} siteName={site.name} domain={site.domain} path={path} />
  <section class="container py-16 md:py-24">
    <a class="link" href="/use-cases">← All use cases</a>
    <p class="editorial-kicker mt-6">Shopify operating playbook</p>
    <h1 class="hero-title mt-5 max-w-5xl">Black Friday email: offers, audiences and peak operations</h1>
    <p class="mt-7 max-w-3xl text-xl leading-9 text-[#4a2d17]">Plan one coordinated sale across campaigns and automations, with enforceable access terms, current purchaser suppression and a named pause owner.</p>
  </section>
  <section class="container pb-12">
    <div class="prose-shopify max-w-4xl">
      <h2 class="font-serif text-3xl font-black text-[#24170f]">Write the offer contract before the calendar</h2>
      <p>Document eligible products, markets, currencies, discount depth, minimum spend, exclusions, shipping terms, start and end times with time zones. Specify whether codes combine with loyalty, subscription or cart offers. Give support the same terms customers see.</p>
      <p>Define what early access means: earlier shopping, a reserved allocation or different pricing. A VIP email label is not an access control. If access must be limited, demonstrate the actual eligibility check at checkout and decide how forwarded links or codes are handled.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="container pb-12">
    <div class="prose-shopify max-w-4xl">
      <h2 class="font-serif text-3xl font-black text-[#24170f]">Build audiences with a clear snapshot policy</h2>
      <p>Define VIP eligibility and sale subscription separately from general newsletter membership. Record when segments were evaluated and which changes must be reflected at dispatch. A recent buyer of the promoted SKU may need exclusion, a relevant cross-sell or information about an existing price-adjustment policy. Do not invent a universal purchase exclusion window.</p>
      <p>Do not restore suppressed contacts just because it is sale week. Review acquisition sources and permissions before including new giveaway or early-access signups. Reconcile counts between the intended segment and the dispatch file; stale segment membership can invalidate the access promise.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="container pb-12">
    <div class="prose-shopify max-w-4xl">
      <h2 class="font-serif text-3xl font-black text-[#24170f]">Budget contact pressure across workflows</h2>
      <p>Put teaser, VIP, public launch, reminder and final deadline messages on one calendar with their audience and purpose. Choose caps using subscriber expectations, prior comparable response and current delivery signals. Another channel is another contact, not free capacity.</p>
      <p>For each automation, mark keep, adapt or pause and assign a restoration owner. Cart offers must respect sale prices and stacking terms. Browse, welcome, loyalty and winback may collide with the campaign. Keep necessary order and service messages available. Cyber Monday continues this contact history rather than resetting it.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="container pb-12">
    <div class="prose-shopify max-w-4xl">
      <h2 class="font-serif text-3xl font-black text-[#24170f]">Design for changing stock and prices</h2>
      <p>Prepare sale and fallback creative using current product prices, eligibility and stock. Verify mobile layout, currency, landing-page terms and checkout redemption. A product block that was accurate at scheduling can be stale at dispatch or open time.</p>
      <p>For a size-run fashion drop, coordinate VIP allocation with public stock. For home goods, validate delivery eligibility and bulky-item exclusions. If a hero SKU sells out, stop pending incompatible sends and use an accurately described alternative; do not keep an urgency headline for unavailable stock.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="container pb-12">
    <div class="prose-shopify max-w-4xl">
      <h2 class="font-serif text-3xl font-black text-[#24170f]">Run a peak operations desk</h2>
      <p>Keep a send ledger with campaign ID, segment definition, scheduled time, actual dispatch progress, owner and pause action. Confirm expected queue throughput with the sender before the event. A scheduled time is not guaranteed receipt time; an expiring offer needs room for actual delivery delays.</p>
      <p>During the event, watch purchase suppression freshness, delivery errors, complaints, stock and support reports. Name who can pause campaigns and dependent automations. Record decisions and the conditions required to resume. Set review frequency to event risk and data latency rather than a fixed six-hour suppression rule.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="container pb-12">
    <div class="prose-shopify max-w-4xl">
      <h2 class="font-serif text-3xl font-black text-[#24170f]">Give reminders a reason to exist</h2>
      <p>A reminder should add a useful fact: a real deadline, eligible category, shipping term or an answer to a common objection. Remove purchasers from irrelevant repeat offers using the current order state. Where another purchase makes sense, explain the different use rather than recycling the same discount.</p>
      <p>Do not use repeated false extensions. If the business changes an end time, update the offer contract, checkout and every queued message. SMS requires its own permission and applicable sending constraints; an unopened email alone does not authorize a text.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="container pb-12">
    <div class="prose-shopify max-w-4xl">
      <h2 class="font-serif text-3xl font-black text-[#24170f]">Plan the post-sale branches</h2>
      <p>Separate gift purchases, self-purchases and subscription orders when information supports it. Gift buyers may need delivery information rather than immediate replenishment. Recent sale customers can receive useful education or service without an automatic deeper discount.</p>
      <p>After a delivery incident, use the <a class="link" href="/use-cases/deliverability">deliverability runbook</a>. A universal promotional pause is not a recovery plan. For non-buyers, decide whether a later <a class="link" href="/use-cases/winback">winback</a> message is relevant and permitted; do not treat every non-purchase as a request for more sale mail.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="container pb-12">
    <div class="prose-shopify max-w-4xl">
      <h2 class="font-serif text-3xl font-black text-[#24170f]">Evaluate contribution over comparable periods</h2>
      <p>Measure revenue net of discounts, returns and refunds, then subtract product, variable fulfillment, messaging and incremental campaign costs. Keep attributed orders separate from incremental orders. Include the cost of capture tools and peak channel volume in the campaign forecast.</p>
      <p>Compare equal-age purchase cohorts for repeat purchase and full-price share. January revenue can change because of product mix, seasonality or acquisition, so a decline alone does not prove November list damage. If testing incremental email impact, predefine assignment, shared sale exposure, exclusions and the outcome window with the <a class="link" href="/use-cases/analytics">reporting owner</a>.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="container pb-12">
    <div class="prose-shopify max-w-4xl">
      <h2 class="font-serif text-3xl font-black text-[#24170f]">Rehearse the failures before scheduling</h2>
      <p>Proposed rehearsal: forward a VIP code to an ineligible staff account and verify the promised access policy. Place an order after segment creation but before dispatch; expect the chosen purchaser exclusion to update. Sell out the featured variant; expect the next batch to hold or use approved fallback.</p>
      <p>Test an expired code, wrong market, duplicate automation, delayed queue and changed sale end time. Check a gift order and subscription renewal through post-purchase branches. Log actual outcomes and unresolved defects; these are acceptance exercises, not claimed merchant performance results.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="container pb-12">
    <div class="prose-shopify max-w-4xl">
      <h2 class="font-serif text-3xl font-black text-[#24170f]">Choose tools and preserve the operational record</h2>
      <p>Require evidence of segment freshness, access enforcement, suppression sharing, queue visibility, pause controls and audit exports. Clarify ownership when capture, email, SMS and inventory live in separate systems. Compare candidates on the same sale rehearsal and projected peak bill rather than unsupported rankings.</p>
      <p>Complete changes when the team can rehearse and roll back them. Pause each replaced sender before enabling its equivalent; shadow evaluation need not send duplicate live mail. Archive creative, offer versions, segment snapshots, incidents and restoration actions for the retrospective. Use <a class="link" href="/use-cases/holiday-gifting">holiday gifting</a> for the distinct gift journey.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
  <FaqSection faqs={faqs} title="Black Friday email FAQ" />
</BaseLayout>
